+# SST7 v0.1.1 output audit
+
+- Uploaded results: 49 cases.
+- Basic overall: 49 INDETERMINATE.
+- Extended overall: 48 INDETERMINATE, 1 FAIL.
+- All 49 basic G00 and G01 gates pass.
+- Extended FAIL: link_0.3.1_final.txt, G00 closure gap 0.196411 > 0.15.
+- Root cause found in v0.1.1 parser: generic TXT loader concatenates all numeric rows and always returns one component. Multi-component links are therefore not segmented.
+- Post-hoc jump segmentation (not blind-certified) turns link_0.3.1 into 3 components with closure gap ratios about 0.00288--0.00300.
+- With post-hoc component segmentation, all 49 cases satisfy extended geometry thresholds. Maximum corrected closure-gap ratio: 0.00606253979. Maximum corrected last-step length relative error: 0.000925560429. Minimum corrected mode correlation: 0.999999588959.
+- G03 did not execute any pairwise linking in the official run because every TXT input was parsed as one component.
+- Post-hoc corrected segmentation yields 44 pairwise Gauss integrals; maximum residual from nearest integer is 0.0316741034.
+- No phase/field/timeseries/probe/repr sidecars were present, hence G10/G11/G20/G21/G22/G30/G31/G40/G50/G51 are indeterminate for all cases.
+- Freeze integrity bug on Windows: run_campaign hashes the in-memory LF JSON string but Path.write_text writes CRLF bytes. Basic freeze records b8cace... while actual opaque_results.json bytes hash to c8cfdf...; extended freeze records 0028f0... while actual bytes hash to a6ff6c.... This is newline normalization, not evidence of tampering, but the freeze verifier is not byte-stable on Windows.
+- Basic/extended holdout partitions are independently randomized because prepare() uses a fresh random seed each run. Basic split is 30 train / 19 holdout; extended is 36 train / 13 holdout. For direct basic-vs-extended comparison, reuse one blind manifest/seed.
